Refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for a description of the "nvinfer"
plugin and "NvDsInfer" API.

TensorRT 11 upgrade:
- Build with matching system TensorRT development headers and libraries. Vendor
  link stubs or copied legacy headers cannot restore removed APIs.
- network-mode=2 requires genuine FP16/mixed arithmetic in the model graph;
  TensorRT 11 no longer converts a FLOAT graph through a builder precision flag.
  Prepare supported sample models explicitly after installation using
  samples/modelopt/prepare_samples.py. Original model filenames are retained.
- network-mode=1 requires an explicitly quantized model. Legacy INT8 calibration
  caches, BEST mode and layer-precision overrides are not supported by this route.
- make also builds nvdsinfer-engine-builder. This is a build-only SDK front end,
  not a general trtexec replacement or a performance benchmark.
- DLA and non-sample model conversions require separate target qualification.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing the plugin:
Export or set in Makefile the appropriate CUDA_VER

Run make and sudo make install

NOTE: To compile the sources, run make with "sudo" or root permission.
